Bene-lux governments a national part of Fortis
The Benelux states will be assisted by the Belgian-Dutch-Dutch-Dutch bank Fortis, which is the first in Europe due to the propagating effect of the U.S.-mortgage crisis, with partial nationalization: the trio of countries will support the monetary and insurance institute, which also has a €11.2-billion-dollar capital participation.
This was agreed this weekend at the highest level by the Belgian, Luxembourg and the Dutch government, with the participation of the President of the European Central Bank and the European Commissioner for Competition.
Fortis is the first in the euro area to enter a major crisis as part of the crisis of international financial markets, which has been circulating in waves for more than a year, and decisions made in this matter could be judged as precedent precedent from some point of view.
In terms of the decision, which was born on Sunday at night, all three states will buy nearly half (49 per cent) of the bank's property.
With absolute certainty, the bank will sell part of its capital gains, in particular - mainly insurance - activities purchased last year from the Dutch bank ABN Amro.
Fortis shares began to fall sharply last week, in the second half of the week there were already serious signs of the crisis at the institute.
Analysts, however, apgree in the fact that with its 85 thousand employees, the bank is too big to let it go bust.
Securities of the company fell by only 12 percent on Friday, to a 14-year low.
Since January, the value of the shares has fallen by more than two-thirds.
In view of the current share prices, the group's total market capital is around 14 billion euros, according to the company's leaders it is unbearable.
After all, the company's management accreviates uncertainty in the overseering overseas market about the collapse of Fortis shares related to the $700-billion-dollar U.S-to-admit plan.
On Monday, the shares rose slightly.
On Friday, a new chief-at-haired CEO Filip Dierckx was appointed to the head of the bank.
A financial institution was also looking for private buyers, but with a more serious offer, no one has ever come forward.
The Belgian government has previously announced that investors don't have to worry, they won't lose their money.
There has been no panic among the bank's clients so far, and the branches have not been taken by an attack.
In Hungary, the Fortis bank has a separate branch and has also purchased several leasing firms.
Fox in chicken corkscrew
Life and health insurers in U.S., based on data on drug purchase data, often reject the possibility of concluding an insuring contract with a bidder.
Data protection experts are concerned that the data market will become uncontrollable.
"There is a data protection protection program that binds the use of drug prescribing data in any event to the consent of the person concerned.
It must be in the hands of someone independent, otherwise we entrust the chicken coop to the fox," Richard Dick, the author of a drug prescribing program, was quoted as saying.
Insurer companies make insurance premiums and amounts disbursed in the event of insured events dependent on the health of interested parties, and if the risk is evaluated as too large, they do not even take out insurance.
Earlier, they dispatched those concerned for medical examinations and concluded the contract only when they knew their results.
Ten years ago Dick devised a much cheaper procedure: on the basis of an identification number from pharmaceuticals, the pharmaceutical customer easily finds out what drugs the person has purchased in the last year and a half, from which the program itself deduces, what the disease suffers and what is his state of health.
For example, if he regularly buys a large number of cholesterol-reducing drugs, this indicates that it has virtually uncontrollably high levels of blood fat, which immediately puts it in the category at a higher risk.
There are several versions of the program circulating, some at the same time determine the coefficient of risk, so there is almost no work to the insurance company, although minor difficulties arise.
Disadvantages include the fact that some drugs can also be used for several purposes, some compounds are, for example, usable against migraines or hot flushes, but are also effective against depressants.
From the point of view of commercial insurers, they represent a significant risk-enhancing factor, whereas the former has not.
In order to request and process the data, special companies have been created to ask the patient for permission before obtaining the necessary information from pharmaceuticals.
They are now being forced by the authorities, even though they have not been punished for their negligence.
In recent times, some companies have already processed the results of laboratory examinations, which combine data on the drugs used, thanks to which they are able to provide an even more accurate picture of the health status of patients.
More and more companies have access to the data, at the same time it will become more and more complicated to control their use.
There is a special law on the protection of data on the state of health, but its effectiveness applies only to providers of health services and insurers.
The bill, which will give the authorities the power to control even businesses specializing in the provision of data, is prior to Congress.
Recognising that that this is not enough: that is why he has developed his program in such a way as to tie it to the express consent of the person in question.
Another thing is that it can hardly deny the permission in question, otherwise the insurers won't conclude a contract with him.
So the hens, after all, are somewhat repulsed on the fox's good will.
The Global Marseilles Menu
The European Union and India will resume commerce reversals
Since the European Union and India are their leading trading partners, this theme dominated, in addition to other, mainly global problems, the Ninth-Stating Summit agenda at the highest level.
A Franco-Indian congrutory summit will also take place today, where it will primarily include cooperation in the field of atomic energy.
The European Union recognizes that India is an emerging democratic power, which should be given a greater opportunity to speak into international affairs, but the member countries have not yet been able to find a common denominator on the issue of support for New Delhi's permanent membership in the United Nations Security Council.
Thus, this question was not further analyzed at the ninth summit held in Marseille.
French President Nicolas Sarkozy, as the current president of the Union and European Commission President José Manuel Barroso and high foreign policy official Javier Solan have welcomed Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh, with whom they have also agreed to double the trade turnover within five-Year-and-Year, or increase to more than a hundred billion euros.
Given that between 2000 and 2007, the exchange of goods has risen from $25 to $55 billion, this is not an over-ambiguous target.
Twenty-six pre-existing bipartisan agreements with India on civil aviation have been aligned from a legal point of view, so air transport was also given the green light in the future.
By the end of 2009, India and the Union would like to sign a free trade agreement.
Sarkozy has vowed that the negotiations would be accelerated.
The aim is to settle the balance sheet, while the EU is India's first trading partner, New Dilli figures in ninth place among the EU's partners up to ninth.
The summit also paid attention to global issues.
Situation in Afghanistan-Pakistan, respectively terrorism - the two sides in all its forms were condemned and called for an expeditiously convection of the United Nations conference.
They have also abolished the end of a round of business negotiations from Doha, although both have a large share in its hitherto failure.
The European Union has confirmed that it will insist on its energy and climatic programme that it would like to reduce emissions of harmful substances by at least 20 per cent by 2020.
India also agreed with this, as well as the fact that at the climate conference for next year it would be necessary to conclude a global agreement and the production of gases causing the greenhouse effect to reduce by 50 per cent by 2050.
Both parties would also like to prevent food prices from rising and support the convening of an international conference to analyze the financial crisis.
The Indian prime minister arrives today in the French capital, where at a two-sided meeting he is going to conclude a trade related to the peaceful use of atomic energy.
Paris is confident that French companies will get a mandate to build India's twenty-bbillion-equill nuclear reactors.
According to agency reports, the agreement should be valid for 15 years.
