Steve Fossett plane found, a million-dollar who disappeared a year ago
Steve Fossett, a million-dollar who vanished on September 3, 2007, has been found while flying the desert in Nevada.
Debris was discovered on one plateau at an altitude of three thousand meters, in the Mammoth Lakes area of Sierra Nevada, on the border between California and Nevada.
There were no human remnants inside the aeroplane.
Sheriff Madera County, John Anderson, dispersed the doubt that still remained: "The plane was found, we've sent a team there, and we're now sure it's exactly what Steve Fossett flocked in on the day he disappeared," he said at a press conference.
The sheriff therefore clarified that there were no human remnants not been found either on the plane or in the surrounding area.
The 63-year-old millionaire has been presumed dead since February.
The U.S. Transportation Safety Office (Ntsb) announced that a few hours after recognieving the rubble, an investigative team was deployed, which eventually identified the plane: it's exactly Bellanca 8kcab, undisclosed since September 3, 2007, when Fossett flew from Yerington in Nevada for a three-h-hour flight.
Yesterday, still in California, not far from Nevada's border, some Fossett's personal items were found with one pair near their dwelling in Mammoth Lakes.
There are two documents with Fossett's name, both issued by the Illinois Federal Aviation Administration, cash and one jacket.
Phossette search was interrupted a month after his disappearance.
